- **The bound — R2** (cry-hstbfhw4; the founder's answer «Файл ребёнка, ключ как у CLI», 2026-11-17, relay
  `.andromeda/runs/2026-11-17T19-03-40Z-wrap/inputs/I1-split-trust-route-adaptation.md.txt`), a boundary widening
  ratified with this bound, binding the plan as worded (directive item 3):
  - viola writes ONLY `projects[<key>].hasTrustDialogAccepted`, for one folder;
  - `<key>` the key the CLI itself writes on an accepted dialog (the git root inside a repository, else the cwd);
  - the file the started child reads — `<CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR>/.claude.json` when viola's home keeps that variable for
    the child (`claude_env_keep`), else the user's `~/.claude.json` — viola reading that ONE environment value for
    that one purpose;
  - only at `run` and `revive`, after the version gate and before the spawn, on a verified CLI, and only when no
    record already trusts the folder;
  - no other key changed, no entry removed, nothing written for the home folder;
  - a file absent, unreadable, a link, not the JSON expected or oversize → viola writes NOTHING (never creates it) and
    the dialog is the human's;
  - one closed word per start in the run log, nothing of the file anywhere;
  - the two security rows saying viola writes nothing into `~/.claude.json` are amended by this entry's own wrap —
    the plan lists them as Expected amendments for the answer card (directive item 3).

- `src/bin/viola-fake-agent.rs` 180–290 — `trusted()` = `--trusted-root` ancestry OR `--trust-config`'s record;
  `record_key` (nearest `.git` ancestor else canonical cwd) and `record_trusts` (bounded read, the exact key only — no
  parent walk); under `--screens` an untrusted cwd draws 2.1.325's trust form.

- `trust-flagonly` — `crates/viola-agent-claude/src/trust.rs`: the flag-only set replaced by a whole-entry insert;
  entry: `cargo nextest run -p viola-agent-claude`; case `flag_only_set_keeps_every_other_key`. With the guard gone an
  existing entry's other keys are lost — unmeasured.

- `trust-home` — `src/trust_record.rs`: the home-folder rule removed; entry: `bash scripts/agent-run.sh run --unit`;
  case `trust_start_home_folder_opens_nothing`. With the guard gone the home folder is written a record — unmeasured.
Each id is at most 16 characters; a `timeout` reading is not «holds».

- (obs) Each start writes exactly one `trust-record` line with a closed `detail` and nothing of the file, every role
  line passing `schemas/diag-line.v1.json` (`contract_diag_schema` in the integration entry;
  `start_trust_words_are_each_a_code_word`).

